hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22241","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Damra ibn Said, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in the Eid. He said: He used to recite Qaf and Iqtarabat."
"22242","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Duali, then al-Jundai, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, that they went out from Makka with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Hunayn. He said: The disbelievers had a lote tree at which they devoted themselves and hung their weapons upon it, called Dhatu Anwar. He said: So we passed by a green, great lote tree. He said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhatu Anwar. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have said, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, as the people of Musa said: Make for us a god as they have gods. He said: You are an ignorant people. These are ways; you will ride the ways of those before you, way by way."
"22243","Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyya, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where hunger afflicts us, so what is lawful for us of dead meat? He said: If you do not eat in the morning, nor drink milk in the evening, nor gather herbs, then you may have it."
"22244","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abd Allah ibn Uthman informed me, from Nafi ibn Sarjis, he said: We visited Abu Waqid al-Bakri, and Ibn Bakr said al-Badri, in his illness in which he died, and he heard him saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the lightest of people in prayer upon the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22245","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Dayli, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, toward Hunayn, and we passed by a lote tree. I said: O Prophet of Allah, make for us this Dhatu Anwar as the disbelievers have Dhatu Anwar, and the disbelievers used to hang their weapons upon a lote tree and devote themselves around it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Greatest; this is as the Children of Israil said to Musa: Make for us a god as they have gods. You will ride the ways of those before you."
"22246","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, that they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where hunger afflicts us, so when is dead meat lawful for us? He said: If you do not eat in the morning, nor drink milk in the evening, nor gather herbs, then you may have it."
"22247","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Duali, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Hunayn, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Mamar, and Mamar is more complete in hadith."
"22248","Abd al-Samad and Hammad ibn Khalid, with the same meaning, said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madina, and therein were people who deliberately cut the rumps of sheep and the humps of camels, so they cut them off. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is cut from the animal while it is alive is dead meat."
"22249","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madina, and the people were cutting off the humps of camels and cutting the rumps of sheep, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is cut from the animal while it is alive is dead meat."
"22250","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Waqid ibn Abi Waqid al-Laythi, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his wives in his Hajj: This, then staying upon the mats."
"22251","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: We used to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when revelation was sent down upon him, and he would narrate to us. He said to us one day: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: We sent down wealth to establish prayer and give zakat, and had the son of Adam a valley, he would love to have a second to it, and had he two valleys, he would love to have a third to them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, then Allah turns to whoever repents."
"22252","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha narrated to me, from the hadith of Abu Murra, that Abu Waqid al-Laythi narrated to him, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, three men passed by. One of them came and found a gap in the circle and sat, and the other sat behind them, and the third went away. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of the news of these men? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: As for the one who came and sat, he sought shelter so Allah sheltered him, and the one who sat behind you was shy so Allah was shy of him, and as for the one who went away, a man who turned away, so Allah turned away from him."
"22253","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Nafi ibn Sarjis, he said: We visited Abu Waqid al-Kindi in his illness in which he died. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the lightest of people in prayer with the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself."
"22254","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, from Nafi ibn Sarjis, he said: We visited Abu Waqid al-Kindi, Ibn Bakr said al-Badri, in his illness in which he died, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22255","Muhammad ibn al-Nushajan, and he is Abu Jafar al-Suwaydi, narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Waqid al-Laythi, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his wives in the Farewell Hajj: This, then staying upon the mats."
"22256","Yunus and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Damra ibn Said, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: Umar, may Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with him, asked me about what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited in the prayer of the two Eids. Surayj said: With what did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in the going-out prayer? He said: So I said: He recited Iqtarabat al-saa wanshaqqa al-qamar and Qaf wal-Quran al-Majid."
"22257","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Nafi ibn Sarjis narrated to us that he entered upon Abu Waqid al-Laythi, the companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his illness in which he died, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the lightest of people in prayer upon the people, and the most constant upon himself, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
